# The overloaded `+` applied to one Int and one String.
#
# `+` is the one operator with more than one signature -- Int + Int and
# String + String -- so it is also the one where "no signature matches"
# has to be reported rather than a single expected type. Neither operand
# is wrong on its own; it is the pair that has no meaning.
#
# This program is expected to FAIL type checking. Its `.out` holds the
# error message, not a program's output.

count = 13
count ++ "hello"
